just four months after the last one  another series of attacks on a European  capital play most worryingly in Brussels  a city that's been the focus of intense  counter-terror activity since Paris  officials across Europe scrambled to  react to this latest outrage above  Downing Street in an act of solidarity  the Belgian flag flown at half-mast  inside a familiar response from the  Prime Minister an attack on them he said  is an attack on all of us these were  attacks in Belgium they could just be  attacks just as well be attacks in in  Britain or in France or Germany or  elsewhere in Europe and we need to stand  together against these appalling  terrorists and make sure they can never  win President Obama has continued his  historic tour of Cuba he's been  criticized for making friends with  America's old enemies while not doing  enough to tackle newer far more  dangerous ones the White House issued  these photographs of the president and  his national security adviser Susan Rice  being briefed on the attacks which he  condemned in a speech to Cubans we will  do whatever is necessary to support our  friend and Ally Belgium in bringing to  justice those who are responsible and  this is yet another reminder that the  world must unite we must be together  regardless of nationality or race or  faith in fighting against the scourge of  terrorism President Obama has insisted  despite Paris Islamic state is being  contained losing power and influence the  pictures from Brussels today suggests  otherwise on a trip to Jordan the e use  foreign policy chief federica mogherini  wasn't able to control her emotions as  she reacted to the news I will stop here  you will understand this today is a  difficulty  in Paris a city still recovering from  attacks that killed 130 last November  the French president Francois Hollande  called on all Europe to show solidarity  with Belgium this is attack en a prayer  door these attacks come after others  Paris was targeted last year in January  and November other continents have been  affected too but we are facing a global  threat which demands a global response  but there are clear limits to that  global response still despite attacks on  Europe in the heart of its cities and no  political appetite for greater military  action against Islamic state on the  ground instead governments are relying  on intelligence and security measures  which have now again been thwarted  Dominic waghorn Sky News
 

